      "description": "Watch Portsmouth vs QPR highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The Championship action heated up as Portsmouth welcomed QPR for a clash filled with tactical intrigue. Both sides looked to establish their dominance early on in this highly anticipated fixture on August 15, 2026 . Early Breakthrough and Momentum Shifts Portsmouth found their rhythm early, and in the 15th minute, Terry Devlin sent the home crowd into raptures. After a brilliant assist from Ebou Adams , Devlin clinicaly finished to put the hosts ahead. The early goal seemed to galvanize the home side, but the momentum was about to shift dramatically as the visitors found their feet. The Ilias Chair Masterclass QPR took full control as the first half progressed, led by a stunning performance from Ilias Chair . In the 33rd minute, Chair equalized after being set up by Harvey Vale . The playmaker then turned provider in the 40th minute, assisting Koki Saito to put the visitors in front. Just before the half-time whistle in the 45+2nd minute, Chair struck again, finishing a pass from Amadou Salif Mbengue to cap off a remarkable turnaround. Tactical Adjustments and Final Whistle The second half was a story of substitutions and defensive discipline rather than goals. Managers introduced fresh legs like Paul Smyth , Glen Kamara , and Marko Milovanovic to alter the game's flow. Despite Portsmouth 's persistent efforts to claw back into the match, the QPR defense held firm through seven minutes of stoppage time to secure the result and take all three points home."
